  "reference_expectations": [
    "Schema validates selected reference shapes only. Current authorization, organization intersection, field projection, cursor binding, endpoint policy and live HTTP behavior require implementation tests.",
    "QueryRequest is the connector-bound request after core authorization: owner_org_refs is explicit, unique and bounded to 1..256 IDs; an empty intersection returns locally without an outbound call. IDs never establish authorization.",
    "QueryPage empty success and QueryFailure are separate union branches. complete does not prove a full snapshot or permit absence deletion; source failure must not fall back to mock.",
    "Device observed_at=null means no observation. Unknown can also carry a real observation time; no universal unknown/null equivalence or stale threshold is invented.",
    "AI ToolInput fields here select only id/human_key/status. Reference time uses the existing AIQueryResponse.sources[].observed_at envelope, not an invented row field. Missing type or unavailable open state requires needs_input, not a broader query.",
    "Risk observations are arrival-ordered, not sequence-sorted. Canonical unsigned decimal strings compare by length then lexical order; the schema checks syntax, never this comparison or checkpoint chronology.",
    "RISK-ARRIVAL: late-high has the larger sequence but observed_at precedes closed_checkpoint.observed_at. It may update applicable transport facts, but must neither create a generation nor change the closed disposition. old-low cannot overwrite a newer source projection.",
    "RISK-ARRIVAL numeric sequence order is old-low then late-high. These are reference expectations, not executable schema proofs; no JS number conversion is allowed."
  ],
